; Checks lib/unicode_tables.ml against what tools/gen_unicode_tables.py produces
; for the Unicode release it names:
;
;     dune build @unicode
;
; and, if it is not, says so with a diff and the command to regenerate. Its own
; alias, and deliberately target-less so that it stays out of @default and @all:
; the generator reads the Unicode Character Database over the network, and a
; build that needs the network is a build that fails in an opam sandbox, in CI
; without egress, and on a train. Pass --ucd <dir> to the script to work from a
; local copy instead.

(rule
 (alias unicode)
 (deps
  (:gen ../gen_unicode_tables.py)
  (:tables %{project_root}/lib/unicode_tables.ml))
 (action
  (run python3 %{gen} --check %{tables})))
